  },
  data: {
    LLM: "1. First Betting: After the initial cards are dealt, the player with the highest card starts the betting.\n2. The Reveal: The dealer turns cards from the undealt deck one at a time.\n3. Matching: If the turned card matches a player's rank, that player takes the card.\n4. Betting Rounds: Every time a match occurs, a new round of betting begins, led by the player with the most cards (or highest rank if tied).\n5. Discards: If a card doesn't match anyone's held rank, it is discarded, and the next card is flipped.",
    Player: "1. First Betting: After the initial cards are dealt, the player with the highest card starts the betting.\n2. The Reveal: The dealer turns cards from the undealt deck one at a time.\n3. Matching: If the turned card matches a player's rank, that player takes the card.\n4. Betting Rounds: Every time a match occurs, a new round of betting begins, led by the player with the most cards (or highest rank if tied).\n5. Discards: If a card doesn't match anyone's held rank, it is discarded, and the next card is flipped.",
    objective: 'Collect all four cards of your starting rank OR hold the lowest total hand when someone else completes their set.',
    gameplay: "1. First Betting: After the initial cards are dealt, the player with the highest card starts the betting.\n2. The Reveal: The dealer turns cards from the undealt deck one at a time.\n3. Matching: If the turned card matches a player's rank, that player takes the card.\n4. Betting Rounds: Every time a match occurs, a new round of betting begins, led by the player with the most cards (or highest rank if tied).\n5. Discards: If a card doesn't match anyone's held rank, it is discarded, and the next card is flipped.",
    keyRules: [
      'Follow the legal action constraints defined for Four of a Kind.',
      'Round outcome is resolved by the scoring method: Scoring summary: Two-pot system: High pot (four-of-a-kind or best hand) and Low pot (lowest 5-card hand).',
      'Winning condition: Collect all four cards of your starting rank OR hold the lowest total hand when someone else completes their set.',
    ],
